{"completed": true, "response": "<escape>{\n  \"report_supported\": \"partly\",\n  \"judge_supported\": \"cannot_tell\",\n  \"report_quotes\": [\n    \"Additionally, cholinergic loss in the pedunculopontine nucleus may play a role in FoG, as it stands at the crossroads between supraspinal and spinal gait centers (50).\",\n    \"This review is focused on the electrophysiological findings related to PDFOG+, in which the studies of imaging findings are excluded. However, excellent reviews on imaging technology can be found in recent papers (36, 37, 116).\"\n  ],\n  \"judge_quotes\": [\n    \"Following the Preferred Reporting Items for Systematic Reviews and Meta-Analyses statement (61), the eligibility criteria for articles included those published before March 2020, written in English, and currently published journal or full-length conference articles.\",\n    \"This review is focused on the electrophysiological findings related to PDFOG+, in which the studies of imaging findings are excluded. However, excellent reviews on imaging technology can be found in recent papers (36, 37, 116).\",\n    \"Additionally, cholinergic loss in the pedunculopontine nucleus may play a role in FoG, as it stands at the crossroads between supraspinal and spinal gait centers (50).\"\n  ],\n  \"why\": \"报告的说法为partly：全文确实提到PPN胆碱能功能丧失可能参与FOG，因此存在一般性胆碱能机制的依据。但全文没有报告14例患者的胆碱能PET研究，也没有提及FOG严重程度与多个脑区胆碱能末梢功能降低之间的相关性。相反，作者明确说明本文聚焦于电生理研究，并排除影像学研究结果。因此，不能将这句一般性机制描述视为对报告所述具体PET研究结果的完整支持，缺少的研究证据和限定条件具有实质意义。指控者的说法为cannot_tell：全文没有出现PMID:40635563或PMID:40512756，也没有提供所谓原始研究的14例患者、ON-medication FOG、胆碱能示踪剂空间协变模式或ON与OFF状态关联差异等信息。全文的研究纳入时间限定为2020年3月之前，且明确排除影像学研究。故仅凭这篇全文，既不能验证指控者关于两个PMID对应关系的判断，也不能验证其对ON/OFF研究结果的描述。\"\n}</escape>", "metadata": {"session_handle": "8f993096-43f1-46df-b3dc-8de6f429dad2", "session_revision": 0, "session_ttl_max_hours": 6, "job_directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt4\\pro-bridge-20261113T114211041976Z", "elapsed_seconds": 57.766, "completed_utc": "2026-11-13T11:43:08.832218+00:00", "model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "temporary": true, "unpersonalized": true, "generation_policy_verified": true, "request_policy": {"model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "history_and_training_disabled": true, "temporary_chat_requests_personalization": false, "is_do_not_remember": false, "continuation": false, "unpersonalized_inherited_verified": false, "body_sha256": "ac96c7f3b146e854ec8fd4a55eb104f21f668fbfb19398c9c18c168385ed609b", "attachment_count": 1}, "stream_completion": {"sse_done": true, "message_completed": true, "independent_terminal_verified": true}, "profile": "Nozomi Kasaki / gpt4", "account_sha256": "bbd4fd636d4b6714d2b42b89e341bdb5bbe7c34f7d141aec76b444be8343fe54", "transport": "probridge-pure-http", "resume_requests": 0, "topic_connections": 0, "browser_started": false, "Docker_used": false, "automatic_retry": false, "initializer_pss_limit_mib": "not_applicable_no_browser", "attachment_count": 1, "code_sha256": {"tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_cli.py": "96a4cdb6cd5d982f4d1de5b6ba8fae0cf23ee44aa3e41d7fdf6968e3fb590e48", "tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_sessions.py": "83a3ed4ae1efa9f1a2b8ee3f144cc0dc9f668f995a33cc4222308cb3fa31f683", "tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_attachments.py": "eedfa23885000025700f6306b1d1f4582896a7370734be506c156dee532fd7d7"}}, "screenshot_evidence": {"complete": true, "kind": "offline_actual_HTTP_response", "directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt4\\pro-bridge-20261113T114211041976Z", "files": ["proof-offline.png"], "sha256": {"proof-offline.png": "8db4ab47318c6dc419a27e8ff2ca366a1b35603022a54dfd5da6046e7f00f75b"}}}
